./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:17:  - Open-source pointer-guide system where a helper cursor follows your cursor to teach unfamiliar interfaces using pictures and voice AI.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:28:- Open-source LLM/agent wiki: a Wikipedia-like shared knowledge base for memory systems, agents, recommendations, and practical AI patterns.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:29:  - Thesis: memory systems and agents are new, important, and moving fast; builders need a living public wiki rather than everyone rediscovering the same little horrors in private.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:33:  - Goal: build and share the practical knowledge base so everyone can build better AI systems.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:59:  - Could start as a personal-use system or narrow service before thinking about broader productization.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:60:- Shared company prompt context system.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:61:  - A shared place for simple, reusable information about company systems, teams, concepts, processes, or other recurring context.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:63:  - Each actual prompt then mostly needs a “how to think” section: the reasoning style, judgement frame, and task-specific instruction, with shared facts supplied separately.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:64:- Migrate Hermes planning/system state onto a real database.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:67:  - Preserve as a system/product idea, not current sprint work.
./migration/source-snapshot/ideas.md:81:  - Possible form: a Hermes skill or a better kickoff prompt that starts with scope checks, then proceeds in stages with explicit check-ins before making big taste/scope calls.
./migration/source-snapshot/deferred.md:16:  - Map timezone/date assumptions around source meeting time, transcript occurrence time, user timezone, candidate windows, resolver prompt dates, and display.
./migration/README.md:79:  system's markdown shapes, maps every status and readiness value and every field per §12,
./migration/README.md:93:prove is that the importer correctly migrates data of the real system's shape to the §12 ground
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/sprint-tracking.md:15:- Hook extra meeting recorders into the plugin system.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/sprint-tracking.md:20:  - Add support for additional meeting recorders through the plugin system so new recorder sources can feed Vylo without one-off integrations.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/sprint-tracking.md:74:- Build notifications as its own system.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/sprint-tracking.md:79:  - Notifications are linked to PWA but should be treated as their own product/system question: what deserves a notification, how delivery works, how permissions behave, and how this connects to personas/calendar context.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/sprint-tracking.md:80:  - Current state: notifications now have a two-layer system: any product event can push to a user with its own copy and deep link, using Apple’s declarative wire format so iOS renders notifications at OS level instead of trusting service-worker rendering.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/daily/2026-07-03/tracker.md:52:- Repo freshness checked: `vylo-convex` `main` is ahead of `origin/main`, has no commits since the 2026-07-03 5am cutoff, and has dirty/untracked landing/personas files modified after the cutoff. Those are current-day context, not old-day completion certificates, despite what the filesystem’s little crown says.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/daily/2026-07-01/overview.md:22:- Repo evidence before the 5am boundary includes the design north-star doc, design-system/frontend merge, and brand-mark commits; waitlist/hero commits after the boundary belong to the next planning day, but do not prove the landing page is done.
./migration/source-snapshot/sprints/current/daily/2026-07-01/tracker.md:7:Public/design readiness: get the landing-page story and waitlist path clear, then support it with design-system direction and app polish.

